# Only matters for `vercel deploy`/`vercel --prod`'s local CLI upload --
# a git-triggered deployment clones straight from GitHub and never reads
# this file at all. Written as defense-in-depth for whenever the CLI path
# gets used again (a preview deploy, local testing, etc.).
#
# Root cause of the 1.8GB CLI upload that hit Vercel's free-tier rate
# limit: .claude/worktrees/ held two full duplicate repo checkouts
# (778MB each) that weren't excluded by .gitignore at the time, so the
# CLI's default gitignore-based upload walker swept them in.
# .vercelignore REPLACES gitignore-based inference entirely once it
# exists (doesn't extend it), so .gitignore's own exclusions are
# repeated below too, or they'd stop applying to CLI uploads.
#
# Note: *.mp4/*.wav here are bare globs, so they also match public/*.mp4
# (let-it-rain-1280x720.mp4, orchards-strip2.mp4 -- real assets normally
# copied into dist/ at build time) -- a `vercel --prod` CLI deploy would
# ship without them. Not a concern for git-triggered deploys (this file
# doesn't apply there), only for the CLI path.

.claude
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.git
supabase
scripts
docs
.tmp-*
*.mp4
*.wav

# Mirror of .gitignore's own exclusions
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
*.local
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.jitsi.example
.s2g-service-role-key
.s2g-keys.json
supabase/.temp/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/
scripts/.contrast-audit.json
.swarm/memory.db
.vercel
